<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's Sideco to be listed in U.S. - report.</title>
<headline>Argentina's Sideco to be listed in U.S. - report.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in Sideco, a construction subsidiary of the SOCMA Argentine industrial group controlled by the Macri family, is due to be launched in New York, daily Clarin reported Monday.</p>
<p>According to Clarin, Sideco will be listed in the United States in order to raise financing for the Macri group's expansion in Brazil.  Sideco is a building company concentrating on public services.</p>
<p>&quot;Sideco will be the group's firm that has the strongest presence in Brazil,&quot; a company source told Clarin.</p>
<p>According to the source, the initial public offering is planned for the end of the year.</p>
<p>((--Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0668))</p>
